# Lines the country test (country.bat) must write to COM1 with
# COUNTRY=049 (scripts/smoke-test): Germany, from \COUNTRY.SYS (the boot
# disk's root, the default) in its default code page, 437. DATE's prompt
# is COMMAND.COM's own, with dashes.

^GRDOS-TEST-BEGIN$
^== COUNTRY$
^COUNTRY 049 DATE 1 TIME 1 CURRENCY "DM" FORMAT 2 DIGITS 2$
^SEPARATORS THOUSANDS "\." DECIMAL "," DATE "\." TIME "\." LIST ";"$
^CODEPAGE ACTIVE 437 SYSTEM 437$
^UPCASE 84 8E$
^Current date is \w{3} \d\d\.\d\d\.\d{4}$
^Enter new date \(dd-mm-yy\): $
^Current time is +\d+\.\d\d\.\d\d,\d\d$
^NLSINFO  COM +544 \d\d\.\d\d\.\d\d +\d+\.\d\d$

# CHCP 850, after NLSFUNC: Germany's 850 data, which keeps the diaeresis
^== NLSFUNC$
^Active code page: 437$
^Active code page: 850$
^COUNTRY 049 DATE 1 TIME 1 CURRENCY "DM" FORMAT 2 DIGITS 2$
^CODEPAGE ACTIVE 850 SYSTEM 437$
^UPCASE 84 8E$
^GRDOS-TEST-END$
